    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-11T04:10:52+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-11T04:10:52+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-10T17:40:52Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-10T17:40:52Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A weak ridge of high pressure develops south of Bight today. This ridge will persist into Thursday before a broad area of low pressure develops over SA on Friday. This low will track eastwards, making way for a new high pressure ridge in the west on Saturday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-11T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-12T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-10T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-11T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers north of Marla, becoming less likely in the late morning and early afternoon. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy. Winds south to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h tending northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the late evening. Daytime maximum temperatures in the high 20s.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 5:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 11 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-12T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-13T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-11T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-12T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Very high chance of showers west of Coober Pedy, medium chance elsewhere. A thunderstorm likely, possibly severe with damaging winds and large hail in the far west. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h in the middle of the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 14 and 21 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-13T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-14T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-12T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-13T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers south of Woomera, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning and afternoon. Winds northwest to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning then tending southwesterly during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 17 and 21 with daytime temperatures reaching 28 to 36.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-14T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-15T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-13T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-14T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower north of Marla, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Coober Pedy in the afternoon and evening. Winds south to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 14 and 18 with daytime temperatures reaching 25 to 32.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
